        question: "What is boot in a 1031 exchange?",
        answer:
          "Boot is any value received in an exchange that is not like kind real property, including cash, net debt relief, or non qualifying personal property. Boot is taxable up to the amount of realized gain, even on an otherwise valid exchange. We help San Jose investors identify every potential boot source before closing.",
